    "interpretation": "OQMD's fingerprint pool is nearly as diverse as MP20_train's by distinct-fraction and n_eff (0.970 vs 0.997 distinct-fraction; n_eff clamps to n in both, i.e. collision pressure is negligible in either single-database pool at this sample size). Cross-database fingerprint OVERLAP is small in absolute terms (1.59% of OQMD's distinct fps also appear in MP20_train's distinct fps; 0.63% of OQMD's distinct fps appear in MP_experimental's) but not zero, and the space-group/crystal-system distributions differ substantially between the two databases (TV distance 0.47 at the 230-space-group level, 0.28 at the 7-crystal-system level; OQMD over-represents cubic symmetry, 51.1% vs MP20_train's 22.9%, likely reflecting OQMD's historical emphasis on high-symmetry intermetallics/alloys). This indicates the fingerprint's collision structure is NOT purely an artifact of MP's particular composition/symmetry distribution -- OQMD, with its own very different symmetry profile, still produces a highly diverse fingerprint pool -- but the two databases are drawn from visibly different structural populations, which matters for M3 below."
