    "verdict": "11/12 marked arms reject after Holm-Bonferroni correction across all 36 tests (12 generators x 3 conditions); 0/24 negative-control arms (unmarked, shuffled-key) reject. The one marked arm that does NOT reject is WyLLM-naive_DFT (n_slots=12, p=0.00317) -- this arm already fails to reject at the raw, uncorrected nominal alpha=1e-3 (0.00317 > 0.001), before any multiplicity correction is applied; Holm correction is therefore not why it fails, it simply never passed. This is the weakest result in the family and is consistent with its very small slot count (n_slots=12) rather than with a failure of marking or of the correction procedure. This reproduces the generator_controls pattern (marked structures are detected, unmarked and shuffled-key controls are not) across every generator corpus for which marking is measurable except this one small, underpowered DFT-relaxed arm, including on both CHGNet-relaxed and DFT-relaxed variants of each generator. This is a null confirmation of generality, not a new phenomenon: the detector's marked/unmarked separation established in generator_controls on the generators tested there holds up when extended to CrystalFormer, WyCryst, WyFormer-harmonic, and WyFormer-letters (both CHGNet and DFT variants) and to MatterGen's DFT-relaxed set, none of which were part of the original generator_controls sample."
